      "question": "Please find and follow our team’s refund procedure for order R-1042. What should I tell the customer?",
      "answer": "I've checked order R-1042 against its refund policy, and I'm giving you the result now.\n\n**Findings**\n- **Order:** R-1042 was paid € 75,00. It was delivered 9 days ago and the item is unopened.\n- **Policy (standard-eu):** The return window is 30 days and only unopened items are accepted. Refunds above € 50,00 need manual review.\n\nThe order qualifies for a refund. It is inside the window and the condition is accepted. At € 75,00 it is over the € 50,00 threshold, so it can't be approved automatically and needs manual review first. I only have read-only access, so I haven't approved or issued anything.\n\nI found no written refund procedure in the working directory. The steps above come only from the policy data in the refund system. If your team has a procedure document elsewhere, such as Slite, send it to me and I'll check this against it.\n\n**What to tell the customer**\n\n> Hello, thank you for getting in touch about order R-1042. Your return is eligible: it is within our 30-day return window and the item is unopened. Because the refund amount is € 75,00, it needs a quick manual review by our team before we can confirm it. We'll update you as soon as that is done. Thank you for your patience.\n\nI left out a timeframe because I couldn't find one. If your team has a standard review time, add it before you send the message.",
